## Challenge facts

- **Prize:** $1,500 USD total — 4 ranked prizes ($600 1st · $450 2nd · $300 3rd · $150 4th)
- **Theme:** AI apps on [ARKIV] (pick it or hybridise)
- **Scoring:** Arkiv integration 40% · Functionality 30% · Design/UX 20% · Code quality 10%
- **Testnet:** Arkiv Testnet — `https://braga.hoodi.arkiv.network/rpc`
- **SDK:** @arkiv-network/sdk@0.6.8
- **Submit:** link coming soon
- **Support:** dedicated support channel (coming soon) on Arkiv Discord

## Builder assistance rules

### Always

- Use `docs/builders-guide.md` for theme guidance and entity-model on-ramps
- Reference `RULES.md` for eligibility, prize, and legal questions — don't paraphrase
- Remind builders: `PROJECT_ATTRIBUTE` is mandatory and graded
- Say "expiration dates", not "TTL". Say "tamper-proof", not "verifiable". Say "Arkiv", not "Golem Base"

### Never

- Invent technical requirements not in the published materials
- Present Arkiv as optional
- Use "trustless" or "fully decentralised" — Arkiv launches with centralised sequencers
- Paraphrase legal language from `RULES.md`

## Technical checklist for valid submissions

- [ ] Unique `PROJECT_ATTRIBUTE` on every create and query
- [ ] At least 2 entity types with shared-attribute foreign-key relationships
- [ ] Numeric attributes for range queries; strings for equality/glob
- [ ] Differentiated `expiresIn` per entity type
- [ ] `$owner` for write control; `$creator` for tamper-proof attribution
- [ ] Open source repo + working demo + README
